Export: send it to a file, because there is nothing to share to.

Import and export were both dead on the Vita, for two different reasons.

Import called `FilePicker.pickFiles`, and `file_picker` has no Vita
implementation. That is fixed outside this app, in `packages/file_picker_vita`,
which registers alongside the other non-endorsed plugins in 0002 and 0003. It
is the first of these plugins that draws its own UI: every platform
`file_picker` supports hands the job to a system dialog, and this console has
none, so the implementation pushes a browser onto the app's own Navigator.

Export never reached a picker at all. keklist offers the choice between saving
to a file and sharing only on Android, and shares everywhere else, so on the
Vita it went straight to `SharePlus.instance.share` and died with
`MissingPluginException(No implementation found for method share on channel
dev.fluttercommunity.plus/share)`.

Sharing cannot be made to work here. `share_plus` has no Vita implementation,
and unlike the file picker there is nothing to build one on: the console has no
system share sheet and no target to hand a file to. Writing a file to the
memory card is the only way data leaves this device.

So on the Vita the action is forced to `saveToFiles` and the choice sheet is
skipped, rather than shown with one live option and one that raises.

Detecting the console is not obvious and is worth recording.
`Platform.operatingSystem` reports "linux" here on purpose, because a truthful
"vita" stops the Flutter framework from starting (see
`patches/dart-sdk/0001-add-vita-host-and-target-os.patch`). So the check asks
the filesystem instead: `app0:` is the running application's own read-only
install mount, present on every Vita and on nothing else. It lives in
`VitaPaths.isVita` so the next app does not have to rediscover it.

Verified on hardware end to end: export writes
`ur0:/data/keklist_export_2026-08-30T08-16-10.zip`, 636 bytes, and importing
that same file back reports "Minds imported: 1".

